WEBVTT

00:00:01.990 --> 00:00:02.990
THE LEFT HALF IS A MONKEY

00:00:02.990 --> 00:00:03.990
THE RIGHT HALF IS A CRAB

00:00:03.990 --> 00:00:04.990
THIS ISN'T A MONKEY-CRAB WAR, NO

00:00:04.990 --> 00:00:05.990
A MONKEY-CRAB FUSION

00:00:14.630 --> 00:00:16.210
RIDDLE

00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:19.630
I'LL GO FROM THE RIGHT

00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:20.880
ARARAGI-SENPAI, YOU GO FROM THE LEFT

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:21.880
Y-YEAH

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:24.090
Araragi-senpai, let's go!

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:25.100
S-Sure!

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:27.470
"BECAUSE I'M LEFT-HANDED,

00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:29.270
SOMETIMES I MISTAKE LEFT AND RIGHT,"
WAS SOMETHING KANBARU DEFINITELY SAID—

00:00:38.230 --> 00:00:38.980
FOR SOME REASON,
SHE WAS SITTING ON THE SWINGS.

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:42.320
WHY IS IT THE MOMENT AN APPARITION
SHOWS UP CHASING AFTER HER,
SHE STARTS PLAYING ON THE PLAYGROUND?

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:44.320
NOT ONLY IS IT UNUSUAL,
IT'S ABSURD, ISN'T IT?

00:00:52.460 --> 00:00:53.210
CRAB

00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:11.100
MY ENTIRE BODY IS CREAKING.

00:01:12.350 --> 00:01:13.810
Wait up, master!

00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:17.770
Use this.

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:22.110
Use it!

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:25.320
<i>The demon sword, "Kokoro Watari"...</i>

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:27.200
There's no need to hesitate.

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:29.620
That thing is an apparition,
but it's also not an apparition.

00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:32.540
It's something bad,
in a state before it turns into an apparition.

00:01:32.540 --> 00:01:34.830
No harm will be done by slaying it.

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:40.000
<i>In the first place,
this sword is not the original,</i>

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:44.590
<i>but a certain person used his own flesh and blood,
and slaved away to create it.</i>

00:01:45.050 --> 00:01:49.220
After all, without a blade,
an armor-clad samurai feels incomplete!

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:52.600
In the end, it's been 400 years
since I lent it to her.

00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:58.560
Kanbaru! Out of the way!

00:02:10.950 --> 00:02:11.870
SNAKE

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:14.830
Araragi-senpai! Look out!

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:16.830
A snake... Jagirinawa?

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:25.090
Ka ka!

00:02:25.510 --> 00:02:27.090
Well done, I guess?

00:02:36.140 --> 00:02:37.730
Sixty-two points.

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:39.290
OWARIMONOGATARI

00:03:39.290 --> 00:03:42.000
SHINOBU MAIL, PART THREE

00:03:43.290 --> 00:03:45.920
That was almost a perfect test
of your prowess, wasn't it?

00:03:46.340 --> 00:03:50.090
Actually, it looks like its specs
were lower than what it used to be.

00:03:50.090 --> 00:03:55.970
When the monkey came up against me by itself,
it was controlling rain.

00:03:55.970 --> 00:03:58.100
That was a troublesome skill.

00:04:09.280 --> 00:04:10.320
Are you all right?

00:04:11.610 --> 00:04:12.660
Are you hurt anywhere?

00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:18.540
I'm not hurt anywhere.

00:04:19.910 --> 00:04:23.170
This is warm.
It smells like you, Araragi-senpai.

00:04:23.380 --> 00:04:26.170
Um, can you not say stuff
that sounds like it's from a romantic comedy?

00:04:26.420 --> 00:04:29.800
But is it okay for me
to be the one wearing this?

00:04:29.800 --> 00:04:34.300
Well... Even in midsummer, standing like this
in the middle of the night can get a bit chilly.

00:04:35.100 --> 00:04:36.550
Well then, hold on just a second.

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:41.690
Wear this.

00:04:46.230 --> 00:04:50.110
I'm really sorry, Kanbaru.
To rope you into something like this.

00:04:50.110 --> 00:04:54.200
In the first place, fighting is forbidden
for basketball players, right?

00:04:54.200 --> 00:04:56.160
You repeat yourself too much, Araragi-senpai.

00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:58.660
If you keep apologizing
so many times like that,

00:04:58.660 --> 00:05:02.660
it makes me doubt
if you really feel bad about all of it.

00:05:05.630 --> 00:05:06.960
Hey, Shinobu.

00:05:14.510 --> 00:05:17.930
Well then. Now, master...
Time to continue the story.

00:05:17.930 --> 00:05:21.850
Continue? Let's see...
what were we talking about?

00:05:21.850 --> 00:05:24.730
I was talking about the pairing, master.

00:05:24.730 --> 00:05:29.360
We were discussing how we needed to recover
the pairing between you and me.

00:05:29.360 --> 00:05:34.360
Otherwise, we'll have a hard time,
even against a defective apparition like that.

00:05:35.570 --> 00:05:39.160
But what does that have to do
with being under the swings?

00:05:39.160 --> 00:05:43.460
As for recovering the pairing...
well, we need to ask some specialist about that.

00:05:43.460 --> 00:05:46.830
You know... For things like this,
experience is the best teacher.

00:05:47.290 --> 00:05:50.840
You should go over there
and lie down in that exact location.

00:05:52.170 --> 00:05:56.090
If you do, there will be things
that you'll gain sight of. Now, let's go!

00:06:10.570 --> 00:06:13.940
<i>Man, this is totally scary!
Scarier than an apparition! What is this?</i>

00:06:14.690 --> 00:06:19.200
<i>What in the world did Shinobu want me to do,
sending me to a land like this?</i>

00:06:19.200 --> 00:06:21.080
<i>What did she want me to understand?</i>

00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:25.540
<i>A bit late now, but I think
the phrase Shinobu wanted to use</i>

00:06:26.750 --> 00:06:28.830
<i>wasn't "Experience is the best teacher,"</i>

00:06:29.960 --> 00:06:33.420
<i>but, "A picture is worth a thousand words."</i>

00:06:38.640 --> 00:06:40.640
CHANGE —> NORTH SHIRAHEBI SHRINE

00:06:47.390 --> 00:06:49.400
"Once I've recovered a bit more,

00:06:49.400 --> 00:06:53.650
I'll come see her to regain
my cherished demon sword 'Kokoro Watari'!

00:06:53.940 --> 00:06:56.360
In the end, it's been 400 years
since I lent it to her.

00:06:56.360 --> 00:06:59.160
Tell her that she should prepare herself
for the late fees!"

00:07:00.320 --> 00:07:03.240
Is that what that samurai said?

00:07:03.240 --> 00:07:07.250
Yeah. And after that,
he took off, laughing boisterously.

00:07:07.250 --> 00:07:08.160
In what way?

00:07:09.290 --> 00:07:12.340
I mean, how did this being laugh?

00:07:12.340 --> 00:07:13.290
Recreate it.

00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:17.550
<i>Recreate it, you ask?
That's more or less asking for the impossible.</i>

00:07:31.100 --> 00:07:32.650
It was something like that.

00:07:35.110 --> 00:07:37.610
Shinobu, could it be...

00:07:37.610 --> 00:07:38.860
Don't worry about it.

00:07:39.070 --> 00:07:41.660
That's impossible.
It's nothing more than a lie.

00:07:41.950 --> 00:07:44.410
A-A lie? But...

00:07:46.950 --> 00:07:50.080
That man died 400 years ago.

00:07:50.080 --> 00:07:52.500
I saw it clearly with my own eyes.

00:07:52.710 --> 00:07:56.960
Even if heaven and earth flip,
even if night becomes day,

00:07:56.960 --> 00:07:58.880
that is one thing
that can't be mistaken.

00:07:58.880 --> 00:08:01.840
It's so stupid
it's not even worth discussing.

00:08:02.140 --> 00:08:03.890
No, but wait, Shinobu...

00:08:04.140 --> 00:08:07.680
If it is the case that this samurai
is pretending to be him,

00:08:07.680 --> 00:08:09.980
it must be due to
something he's planning.

00:08:12.520 --> 00:08:16.690
His objective may be to get myself
or you feeling uneasy.

00:08:16.690 --> 00:08:19.820
That's why you shouldn't worry about it.
It's inevitable.

00:08:19.820 --> 00:08:24.490
No matter what the objective is,
that demon sword, the Apparition Killer...

00:08:26.080 --> 00:08:28.330
I don't intend to hand it over to anyone.

00:08:28.330 --> 00:08:32.170
If he says that he's the mastermind behind
that menagerie that started with the monkey,

00:08:32.170 --> 00:08:35.420
next time, I will personally slay him.

00:08:35.880 --> 00:08:38.170
And I have nothing more to say about that.

00:08:49.640 --> 00:08:53.230
Hey, Koyomin.
I'm glad we finally got to meet up.

00:08:55.610 --> 00:08:57.480
ULTRA ABSOLUTE SUPER RARE

00:08:58.980 --> 00:09:00.360
Well, that's the end.

00:09:01.320 --> 00:09:03.660
A quick message to Yotsugi...

00:09:03.910 --> 00:09:06.410
Saying I safely met up
with Koyomin and company.

00:09:06.410 --> 00:09:08.990
This is why I made her carry
a cellphone for children.

00:09:10.120 --> 00:09:15.710
It seems that doll wasn't herself
with regard to worrying about your well-being.

00:09:15.710 --> 00:09:19.420
It seems... Or rather,
it's pretty obvious if one looks at your face.

00:09:19.630 --> 00:09:20.300
Face?

00:09:20.510 --> 00:09:22.800
Koyomin is in high spirits.

00:09:22.800 --> 00:09:24.050
SEND

00:09:25.010 --> 00:09:27.050
Okay, sorry to make you wait.

00:09:27.600 --> 00:09:31.810
Hello, Ms. Shinobu Oshino,
Ms. Suruga Kanbaru.

00:09:37.190 --> 00:09:39.570
I'm Izuko Oshino.

00:09:39.570 --> 00:09:41.070
You are familiar...

00:09:42.150 --> 00:09:44.610
...with Oshino Meme. I'm his little sister!

00:09:47.320 --> 00:09:52.080
<i>To the lie that was told so audaciously,
I was at a loss of words.</i>

00:09:52.080 --> 00:09:53.080
NO, THAT'S NOT IT.

00:09:53.080 --> 00:09:54.210
YOUR LAST NAME IS GAEN, RIGHT?

00:09:59.040 --> 00:10:03.090
Oh, to think that the Hawaiian-shirt boy
had a younger sister.

00:10:03.090 --> 00:10:04.970
Now that you mention it,
there is a resemblance.

00:10:06.430 --> 00:10:08.470
<i>Shinobu was fooled.</i>

00:10:11.470 --> 00:10:12.970
I get that a lot!

00:10:13.270 --> 00:10:16.770
Yeah. It seems my pitiful big brother
caused you guys a lot of trouble.

00:10:16.770 --> 00:10:18.730
I'm sorry about that.

00:10:20.110 --> 00:10:22.150
I'm Suruga Kanbaru.

00:10:22.150 --> 00:10:24.190
My occupation is Araragi-senpai's...

00:10:25.450 --> 00:10:26.490
...sex slave!

00:10:26.490 --> 00:10:30.280
You... really use that profile
to describe yourself to everyone?

00:10:31.280 --> 00:10:33.370
I see, a sex slave, huh?

00:10:33.370 --> 00:10:35.750
It's so nice to be as young
as you are uninhibited!

00:10:37.460 --> 00:10:40.250
Well then, let's get to the main subject, folks.

00:10:41.000 --> 00:10:42.500
I'm talking about business.

00:10:42.920 --> 00:10:48.090
First off, tell me the tales
of your adventures leading up to here.

00:10:48.090 --> 00:10:51.850
Tell me your entire story,
down to the finest detail.

00:10:52.260 --> 00:10:56.350
Big Sister here loves hearing stories
about someone else's life.

00:10:57.270 --> 00:11:00.020
<i>Coming this far,
there was no reason to gloss over things.</i>

00:11:00.310 --> 00:11:03.610
<i>I told her of tonight's events,
just as they happened.</i>

00:11:04.070 --> 00:11:06.650
It really shows that you're used
to telling stories, Koyomin.

00:11:06.650 --> 00:11:08.070
That was very interesting.

00:11:08.070 --> 00:11:10.240
It's as if you were a professional storyteller.

00:11:10.240 --> 00:11:11.240
A handsome man
being a professional storyteller.

00:11:11.240 --> 00:11:12.240
PROFESSIONAL STORYTELLER (KOUDANSHI)

00:11:12.620 --> 00:11:13.740
That's what it is.

00:11:17.040 --> 00:11:18.500
I'll start with my conclusion.

00:11:18.870 --> 00:11:21.170
That armor-clad samurai, 400 years ago,

00:11:21.170 --> 00:11:24.300
is the first minion that Shinobu's previous self,
the legendary vampire,

00:11:24.300 --> 00:11:29.340
a rare species, the iron-blooded, hot-blooded,
and cold-blooded vampire,

00:11:29.340 --> 00:11:31.590
the Apparition Killer
and King of Apparitions,

00:11:31.590 --> 00:11:37.600
Kiss-shot Acerola-orion Heart-under-blade,
created by drinking his blood.

00:11:38.890 --> 00:11:42.060
In other words, Koyomi Araragi,
you became the second minion

00:11:42.060 --> 00:11:45.360
when Shinobu drank your blood
back during spring break.

00:11:45.360 --> 00:11:47.240
So he would be your senior.

00:11:47.440 --> 00:11:52.200
In that he was the original Apparition Killer,
I guess he'd be Shinobu's senior as well?

00:11:57.080 --> 00:11:58.660
Hey, master.

00:11:58.960 --> 00:12:01.210
This one is unbelievably amateurish.

00:12:01.210 --> 00:12:04.670
Is this one really the little sister
of Hawaiian shirt boy?

00:12:05.000 --> 00:12:07.380
Tell her! Tell her, master!

00:12:07.380 --> 00:12:10.130
Be blunt, in a sadistic way!

00:12:10.130 --> 00:12:13.680
Correct this misunderstanding
that this super-novice has!

00:12:13.680 --> 00:12:14.890
S-Sure...

00:12:15.930 --> 00:12:17.430
B-But, Ga—

00:12:17.430 --> 00:12:19.020
Just call me Izuko.

00:12:19.480 --> 00:12:20.520
...Ms. Izuko.

00:12:20.890 --> 00:12:22.940
I'm saying, just Izuko is fine.

00:12:22.940 --> 00:12:27.860
But Ms. Izuko, Shinobu's first minion
should already be long dead.

00:12:27.860 --> 00:12:30.530
Shinobu witnessed it firsthand.

00:12:32.410 --> 00:12:33.990
<i>Despite turning into a vampire,</i>

00:12:33.990 --> 00:12:36.790
<i>he exposed himself to the sun
to commit suicide by burning himself.</i>

00:12:37.160 --> 00:12:40.540
<i>He burned up, and turned into ashes... So...</i>

00:12:40.830 --> 00:12:45.210
So... He's no longer here.
There's no way that he can be here.

00:12:45.210 --> 00:12:50.220
It's impossible for that armor-clad samurai
to be Shinobu's first minion.

00:12:51.590 --> 00:12:52.550
Why?

00:12:53.590 --> 00:12:54.680
Well, I said—

00:12:54.680 --> 00:12:57.140
Why? Why do you think it's impossible?

00:12:58.970 --> 00:13:00.140
Araragi-senpai...

00:13:00.480 --> 00:13:05.360
But, if you say that,
isn't he an immortal vampire that can't die?

00:13:06.360 --> 00:13:08.860
That's right, Ms. Suruga Kanbaru.

00:13:08.860 --> 00:13:11.360
As expected from someone
who could animate the Monkey's Paw.

00:13:11.610 --> 00:13:13.360
That's outstanding.

00:13:13.660 --> 00:13:17.120
In other words, although it took him
400 years from his suicide by burning,

00:13:17.120 --> 00:13:20.500
said vampire has fully revived.

00:13:20.790 --> 00:13:24.290
To think he can be revived
even if he's turned into ashes and bones...

00:13:24.290 --> 00:13:26.420
I guess I should say,
as expected from the first minion

00:13:26.420 --> 00:13:32.880
chosen by the legendary vampire,
Kiss-shot Acerola-orion Heart-under-blade.

00:13:34.680 --> 00:13:36.300
Now, please observe.

00:13:36.850 --> 00:13:38.810
As I stated the conclusion first,

00:13:38.810 --> 00:13:43.140
I'll go in order,
and explain chronologically.

00:13:43.520 --> 00:13:46.520
Of course, the sun is the vampire's weakness.

00:13:46.980 --> 00:13:49.020
Even grade-school kids know that.

00:13:49.020 --> 00:13:53.070
Even the iron-blooded, hot-blooded,
and cold-blooded vampire

00:13:53.070 --> 00:13:58.530
Kiss-shot Acerola-orion Heart-under-blade
isn't immune to that.

00:13:58.830 --> 00:14:01.200
Not to mention, her minions as well.

00:14:01.580 --> 00:14:03.290
But it's not an exaggeration...

00:14:03.290 --> 00:14:06.000
The King of Apparitions,
whose name was known worldwide,

00:14:06.000 --> 00:14:08.420
isn't an exception, but merely
outside conventional boundaries.

00:14:08.750 --> 00:14:11.670
The weakness wasn't functioning
as a weakness.

00:14:11.920 --> 00:14:14.550
It's a fact that Koyomin,
back in spring break,

00:14:14.550 --> 00:14:17.550
you burst into flames
basking in sunlight, right?

00:14:17.760 --> 00:14:20.310
But you fully recovered after that as well?

00:14:20.640 --> 00:14:21.810
I know that.

00:14:22.100 --> 00:14:25.060
Something similar happened
to the first minion as well.

00:14:25.310 --> 00:14:26.730
That's what this means.

00:14:26.730 --> 00:14:29.860
Of course, in his case, unlike Koyomin
who mistakenly exposed himself,

00:14:29.860 --> 00:14:33.740
he intentionally exposed himself
to the sun in order to kill himself.

00:14:33.740 --> 00:14:37.070
So it's not an attempted (misui) suicide,
but more like a suicide that missed (misu).

00:14:37.610 --> 00:14:41.200
And of course, it seems it took him
a bit of time to revive.

00:14:41.830 --> 00:14:44.080
Roughly 400 years or so.

00:14:44.290 --> 00:14:48.460
To be more precise, even 400 years
after the missed suicide attempt,

00:14:48.460 --> 00:14:53.340
even now, the first one's body
hasn't fully recovered.

00:14:53.960 --> 00:14:58.220
Koyomin, you must've realized this,
as you've directly dealt with the armor-clad samurai.

00:14:58.220 --> 00:15:02.600
You must've felt that the armor-clad samurai
was getting stronger as time went on.

00:15:02.600 --> 00:15:05.600
But to be precise, he wasn't getting stronger.

00:15:06.180 --> 00:15:07.480
He was recovering.

00:15:07.890 --> 00:15:09.980
His health is taking a turn for the better.

00:15:10.310 --> 00:15:12.730
He is trying to get back
to his complete self.

00:15:13.530 --> 00:15:18.740
The reason why he performed an energy drain
on you and Ms. Suruga Kanbaru is, right,

00:15:18.740 --> 00:15:21.030
to try and fix himself up by eating.

00:15:21.030 --> 00:15:24.040
Just like how Shinobu
ate that imitation apparition

00:15:24.040 --> 00:15:27.500
to recover from being scratched
by that imitation apparition.

00:15:27.790 --> 00:15:31.330
Shall I say you're
an admirable second one, Koyomin,

00:15:31.330 --> 00:15:35.760
since you aided the speedy recovery
of the first one?

00:15:36.050 --> 00:15:40.590
No, wait. I'm not just talking about
what happened tonight.

00:15:40.590 --> 00:15:45.020
I'm saying this based off of you as an individual,
looking at all of your recent behavior.

00:15:45.310 --> 00:15:47.600
You don't understand
what I'm talking about?

00:15:47.600 --> 00:15:50.020
It's fine, you'll understand soon enough.

00:15:50.520 --> 00:15:57.280
On the other hand, I wanted to end it all
before it resulted in something like this.

00:15:57.280 --> 00:16:00.030
I was going to have Yotsugi
take care of it all by herself.

00:16:00.700 --> 00:16:03.660
There ended up being
all sorts of miscalculations.

00:16:03.660 --> 00:16:08.540
The fact that I know everything
doesn't mean that everything will go my way.

00:16:08.750 --> 00:16:10.040
Especially involving you, Koyomin.

00:16:10.290 --> 00:16:12.750
Someone like you that doesn't move
according to logic,

00:16:12.750 --> 00:16:16.550
someone whose activities are unpredictable,
an aberrant youth.

00:16:16.760 --> 00:16:20.680
That's why I took responsibility
for making mistakes in my calculations,

00:16:20.680 --> 00:16:22.590
came all the way out to the front line,

00:16:22.590 --> 00:16:25.680
and that's why I asked you
for your assistance.

00:16:25.970 --> 00:16:33.940
You may be thinking that an ill-spirited big sister
is roping you into some troublesome work.

00:16:34.190 --> 00:16:37.440
But the big sister is, in fact,
giving you a chance.

00:16:37.820 --> 00:16:42.200
The perfect chance to claim responsibility
for happenings you set up.

00:16:42.450 --> 00:16:45.450
Though you may not be convinced
of this right away.

00:16:45.780 --> 00:16:48.950
You may never be convinced of it
in your lifetime.

00:16:49.200 --> 00:16:53.420
But Koyomin,
have you never wondered about it?

00:16:53.420 --> 00:16:55.500
About why, for the past six months,

00:16:55.500 --> 00:16:58.960
you've encountered phenomenon
involving apparitions almost monthly?

00:16:59.420 --> 00:17:01.220
You never thought it strange?

00:17:01.510 --> 00:17:07.430
Why did the legendary vampire
Kiss-shot Acerola-orion Heart-under-Blade

00:17:07.430 --> 00:17:13.230
visit the town you live in during spring break,
instead of anywhere else in this world?

00:17:13.600 --> 00:17:15.400
Was it just a coincidence...

00:17:15.400 --> 00:17:22.490
that a crab girl, a snail girl, a monkey girl,
and a snake girl were all in this town?

00:17:22.740 --> 00:17:27.660
The one that Kagenui, an underclassman
that even I have trouble with, went after...

00:17:27.660 --> 00:17:32.500
Was it just a coincidence that the phoenix apparition
lived right here in this town?

00:17:33.040 --> 00:17:37.000
The cat... Has a slightly special circumstance, though.

00:17:37.420 --> 00:17:43.050
That's probably why the armor-clad samurai
accidentally stomped on the tail of a tiger.

00:17:43.050 --> 00:17:47.260
Well, in that regard,
coincidence has favored you.

00:17:47.760 --> 00:17:49.220
A tiger, huh...

00:17:50.640 --> 00:17:54.520
For the first one,
whose entire body became a fireball,

00:17:54.520 --> 00:17:58.060
flames and blazes
must have been traumatic.

00:17:58.060 --> 00:18:01.030
Of course he'd choose a momentary retreat.

00:18:01.480 --> 00:18:04.200
If you live to meet
Tsubasa Hanekawa again,

00:18:04.200 --> 00:18:06.160
make sure to properly thank her.

00:18:07.410 --> 00:18:09.780
You don't know
what I'm talking about now, either?

00:18:10.120 --> 00:18:12.540
Then you don't have to worry about it for now.

00:18:12.950 --> 00:18:19.630
Your friend is nothing more than a sad girl
who protects you, even if it's unintentionally.

00:18:19.920 --> 00:18:23.920
It seems, Koyomin,
your train of thought is that

00:18:23.920 --> 00:18:28.760
something that happens to you
could happen to anyone else.

00:18:28.760 --> 00:18:34.810
To this train of thought that denies miracles,
I do sense quite a bit of modesty,

00:18:34.810 --> 00:18:37.650
but it has one major flaw.

00:18:37.650 --> 00:18:38.650
FLAW

00:18:38.940 --> 00:18:48.070
A huge flaw that makes you say, "You're wrong,"
to convict someone that thinks you're special.

00:18:49.370 --> 00:18:51.660
I'm sorry I'm saying
so many vague things.

00:18:51.990 --> 00:18:56.120
When faced with a young man
in high spirits like you,

00:18:56.120 --> 00:19:00.250
Big Sister here really wants
to explain the meaning of life.

00:19:02.000 --> 00:19:04.550
If this was Big Brother Meme, he'd probably say,
"You seem to be in good spirits.

00:19:04.550 --> 00:19:09.340
Did something nice happen to you,
or something?" and let it end there, but...

00:19:09.340 --> 00:19:14.270
Resentfully enough, yours truly
isn't as tolerant as that immature man.

00:19:15.480 --> 00:19:19.230
Come to think of it, I promised
to explain chronologically, didn't I?

00:19:19.600 --> 00:19:21.480
Then let's keep that promise.

00:19:21.980 --> 00:19:27.740
In the end, keeping the promise
is the shortest route to getting results.

00:19:29.070 --> 00:19:30.910
First, 400 years ago.

00:19:30.910 --> 00:19:32.530
Currently Shinobu Oshino,

00:19:32.530 --> 00:19:39.420
Kiss-shot Acerola-orion Heart-under-blade,
as a vampire, hadn't made any minions until then.

00:19:39.420 --> 00:19:41.750
But that was when she made her first slave.

00:19:42.130 --> 00:19:43.750
She drank human blood.

00:19:44.300 --> 00:19:49.930
The background story of how she ended up
in that situation can be skipped, right?

00:19:50.220 --> 00:19:54.390
It was already told in another location,
and that is a story of the past.

00:19:54.720 --> 00:19:57.640
For you, and for him.

00:19:58.180 --> 00:20:03.060
Going from being a specialist in defeating
apparitions to someone to be exterminated,

00:20:03.060 --> 00:20:05.980
the first one couldn't
tolerate the circumstances.

00:20:06.530 --> 00:20:10.240
He couldn't face the reality
that he had turned into a monster.

00:20:10.240 --> 00:20:12.620
That was why he chose death for himself.

00:20:13.030 --> 00:20:15.450
He exposed himself to the sun.

00:20:16.040 --> 00:20:18.750
He turned into ashes, and was blown
into the wind and disappeared...

00:20:19.160 --> 00:20:20.290
Or so it seemed.

00:20:20.790 --> 00:20:23.500
Leaving Heart-under-blade all his grudges

00:20:23.500 --> 00:20:27.590
and a replica of the Apparition Killer,
the demon blade "Kokoro Watari"...

00:20:28.010 --> 00:20:30.050
Everyone lived happily ever after.

00:20:30.340 --> 00:20:33.050
As stated earlier,
that's not how things went.

00:20:33.470 --> 00:20:36.850
Even turning to ash,
even becoming nothing, he didn't die.

00:20:36.850 --> 00:20:39.520
He may have disappeared,
but he wasn't eradicated.

00:20:39.520 --> 00:20:41.810
He died, but couldn't fully die.

00:20:42.350 --> 00:20:44.230
He kept living.

00:20:44.230 --> 00:20:47.070
He became nothing,
he became the void, and lived on.

00:20:47.610 --> 00:20:53.490
Taking 400 years, so much time
that one feels overwhelmed and even disgusted,

00:20:53.490 --> 00:20:57.040
he slowly, ever so slowly,
recovered his physical form.

00:20:58.950 --> 00:21:01.710
Each time he recovered,
the sun would burn him.

00:21:01.710 --> 00:21:04.080
Each time he constructed,
he was shattered.

00:21:04.080 --> 00:21:08.840
Even then, he didn't give up,
his will was never bent... And he recovered.

00:21:09.380 --> 00:21:15.890
For an astoundingly long time,
the futile trial-and-error for recovery continued.

00:21:16.350 --> 00:21:21.890
Of course, that first one had turned into ash,
so there shouldn't have been a clear will or anything.

00:21:21.890 --> 00:21:25.730
So such a recovery could be called
the reaction of a living vampire,

00:21:25.730 --> 00:21:28.320
or maybe an involuntary response.

00:21:30.240 --> 00:21:33.360
At that point, it seems more pitiful than futile.

00:21:33.610 --> 00:21:37.370
Continuing a game an infinite amount of times,
but never being able to finish the game.

00:21:37.620 --> 00:21:41.750
Because he inherited the immortality of vampires
in a halfhearted way,

00:21:41.750 --> 00:21:43.870
he wasn't even able to die.

00:21:44.290 --> 00:21:46.790
This was eternal life in its true sense.

00:21:47.130 --> 00:21:49.170
If Yoduru had been there,

00:21:49.170 --> 00:21:51.670
I'm sure she would've done
a splendid job of laying him to rest.

00:21:51.670 --> 00:21:54.880
But this is a story about 400 years ago, after all.

00:21:55.140 --> 00:22:04.770
In any case, repeatedly going through
a closed-circuit reincarnation over and over by himself...

00:22:04.770 --> 00:22:08.310
...he might have done so
for the rest of time.

00:22:08.860 --> 00:22:11.360
The first Apparition Killer
had above-average persistence.

00:22:12.240 --> 00:22:14.030
It was definitely worthy of the fact

00:22:14.030 --> 00:22:17.240
that the legendary vampire chose him
as her first minion.

00:22:18.070 --> 00:22:21.540
With a will that wasn't supposed to be there,
with what little willpower he had,

00:22:21.540 --> 00:22:23.790
he rode the wind as ash.

00:22:24.080 --> 00:22:26.290
Even if he was scattered,
he'd congregate once again.

00:22:26.620 --> 00:22:28.790
Grain by grain, with much persistence...

00:22:29.130 --> 00:22:32.300
By perseverance alone,
he returned to this town.

00:22:35.720 --> 00:24:20.187
That was what happened 15 years ago.
